<title>PERU: Banco Santander to issue $20 mln of bonds.</title>
<headline>Banco Santander to issue $20 mln of bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish-owned Banco Santander de Peru plans to issue $20 million of bonds in the near future to finance loan operations, Peru's Stocks and Securities Board (CONASEV) said Monday.</p>
<p>The board said the issue would be split into two series, both of $10 million. CONASEV officials could not give interest rates or other details of the issue.</p>
<p>Banco Santander del Peru, a subsidiary of Banco Santander , is the sixth largest among Peru's 23 private banks.</p>
<p>((-- Eduardo Orozco, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
